  "screened_from": "package_only",
  "eligible_design": true,
  "eligible_reason": "Staggered binary treatment: the opening of a major e-commerce firm's fulfillment center (FC) in a county switches on a treatment indicator for retail workers (worker-quarter panel) and retail establishments (establishment-year panel) located in that county (exc0 versions) or within 100 miles excluding FC counties (exc100 versions). FC openings occur in 50 counties at 23 distinct quarters 1997Q4-2016Q4 (shock_county_year.dta); the regression samples keep openings from 2010 onward (39 counties, 7 opening years; 31-37 county clusters per log). Tables 2-4 are linear TWFE with worker and calendar-quarter fixed effects (lfe::felm, cluster by FC id) and no covariates; Table 3-4 variants replace quarter FE with firm x quarter and/or region x quarter FE (time-invariant characteristics x time, allowed if FirmID is fixed within worker). Tables 6-7 are reghdfe with establishment FE + census-division x year + NAICS x year FE, clustered by county, no covariates. Regression samples contain only ever-treated units (sum_treatment > 0; shock_year != .), so comparison comes from not-yet-treated units; some early-2010 cohorts are always treated in the 2010+ window. Ineligible: Table 3 col 4 and Table 8 (triple differences with retail/trucking/restaurant treatment indicators and county x quarter FE), Table 5 (treatment x low/high subgroup interactions). Figure 4 is an event study of log income in half-years around FC opening, shipped only as coefficient files.",
  "design_notes": "Package replication_package_MS-INS-20-03862 (from the valid _archive zip; the primary mnsc.2023.4795.zip is truncated). Worker data (Tables 1-5, Figures 4-6) are from an unnamed credit bureau and are proprietary: Worker_Data_Regression.dta and Credit_Data_Regression.dta are 24- and 28-row pseudo datasets with masked variable names; Table2-5.R are pseudo codes. NETS establishment data (Tables 6-7, Figure 3) are licensed: NETS_Data_Regression.dta and Retail-NETS.dta are 100-row random samples. QCEW county-industry data (Table 8) are public and complete (QCEW_Data_Regression.dta, 5.78M rows) but Table 8 is a triple-difference. FC opening dates from MWPVL (FC_SHOCK_QTR.dta, FC_SHOCK_YR.dta, shock_county_year.dta) are included. Stata logs for Tables 6-8 (Logs/*.smcl) contain the full regression output.",
  "estimators_reported": ["twfe_static", "twfe_event_study", "triple_difference"],
  "main_or_robustness": "main",
  "n_eligible_specs": 46,
  "n_eligible_specs_note": "Table 2: 6; Table 3: 6; Table 4: 8; Table 6: 8; Table 7 (age cuts): 8; Table 7 (size cuts): 8; Figure 4 event studies: 2.",
